############################################################


>>> You probably just want to run build_and_run.sh <<<

Remember to make a copy of "my_private_details.sh.example"
and set the phone's serial (i.e. name) and watch address.



Most changes are in:
~/android/xDrip/app/src/main/java/com/eveningoutpost/dexdrip/services/Ob1G5CollectionService.java
~/android/xDrip/app/src/main/java/com/eveningoutpost/dexdrip/g5model/Ob1G5StateMachine.java

with FLAG_IMMUTABLE (for newer Android versions) changes in:
~/android/xDrip/app/src/main/java/com/eveningoutpost/dexdrip/utilitymodels/Notifications.java

############################################################

Devices:

Sony Xperia 1 VII at $PHONE_SERIAL ("adb devices" gives you this) 

Galaxy watch 4 (SM-R880) is connected via Wifi debugging at $WATCH_ADDRESS.
It's something like 192.168.0.x:y where x and y are integers.

############################################################

Tested on:

Sony Xperia 1 VII : Android 16, software version 17.1.A.2.265
Samsung Galaxy 4 watch (model SM-R880) : One UI 8.0 software version R880XXS2JZG3 SM-R880X2SAXAA

Installation platform:
Ubuntu Linux 24.04 running Android Debug Bridge version 1.0.41, Version 34.0.4-debian, Installed as /usr/lib/android-sdk/platform-tools/adb, Running on Linux 6.8.0-142-generic (x86_64)

This was developed on a laptop bought on STFC grant ST/R000603/1.
Yes, it's an old device, but thanks STFC - you're literally life savers!

############################################################

# build
nice ./gradlew --no-daemon assembleProdDebug -PappName="$APP_NAME"

# install
adb -s "$PHONE_SERIAL" install -r app/build/outputs/apk/prod/debug/app-prod-debug.apk

# enable (if disabled overnight)
adb -s "$PHONE_SERIAL" shell pm enable com.eveningoutpost.dexdrip.debug

# stop all
adb -s "$PHONE_SERIAL" shell am force-stop com.eveningoutpost.dexdrip
adb -s "$PHONE_SERIAL" shell am force-stop tk.glucodata
adb -s "$PHONE_SERIAL" shell am force-stop com.eveningoutpost.dexdrip.debug

# clean logs
adb -s "$PHONE_SERIAL" logcat -c

# start debug xdrip
adb -s "$PHONE_SERIAL" shell monkey -p com.eveningoutpost.dexdrip.debug 1

# obtain a useful debug, continuously
adb -s "$PHONE_SERIAL" logcat -v time | tee xdrip-direct-connect-test.log


############################################################

# restart bluetooth
adb -s "$PHONE_SERIAL" shell svc bluetooth disable
sleep 3
adb -s "$PHONE_SERIAL" shell svc bluetooth enable

############################################################

# filtered log
adb -s "$PHONE_SERIAL" logcat -v time | grep --line-buffered -E 'Ob1G5CollectionService|Ob1G5StateMachine|KEKS-Plugin|Connecting with auto|Got scan result|Full success|Could not authenticate|Got glucose|Bond|Pair'|grep -v FastPair

############################################################

# disable debug build
adb -s "$PHONE_SERIAL" shell pm disable-user --user 0 com.eveningoutpost.dexdrip.debug

# start juggluco and normal xdrip
adb -s "$PHONE_SERIAL" shell monkey -p tk.glucodata 1
adb -s "$PHONE_SERIAL" shell monkey -p com.eveningoutpost.dexdrip 1

############################################################

# build wear apk
nice ./gradlew --no-daemon :wear:assembleProdDebug -PappName="$APP_NAME"

# install wear apk
adb -s "$WATCH_ADDRESS" install -r wear/build/outputs/apk/prod/debug/wear-prod-debug.apk

# watch wear log
adb -s "$WATCH_ADDRESS" logcat | grep -iE 'dexdrip|wear|message|dataitem'

